  "interpretation": [
    "The known-target FHD/4K/FHD endpoint uses 21.24 MiB less RSS with one retargeted worker than with reopening.",
    "The Source/FHD/4K/FHD endpoint uses 40.13 MiB more RSS with one retargeted worker; the final source-size endpoint is also worse.",
    "After dropping the final Source frame, retarget RSS remains 8.98 MiB higher, while accounted in-use bytes are nearly equal and free arena bytes are 10.63 MiB higher. This is consistent with extra arena retention, not proof of leaked live pixel owners.",
    "No general memory improvement is established; production client target wiring is not enabled by these observations."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "These are last/min/max RSS samples for finite isolated phases, not 120-second whole-shell measurements.",
    "Only latest-frame capacity is instrumented; old-last-good and in-flight frame ownership are not separately measured.",
    "Publications/PTS/loop validation do not establish display FPS or physical presentation.",
    "Allocator counters overlap other memory scopes and do not form an additive RSS ledger."
  ],
  "whole_shell_memory_target_accepted": false,
